.staged-libs/

# Item definitions and models are build output: 26.2 commits generated/data and
# generated/.cache but never generated/assets, and a fresh checkout regenerates them
# with runDatagen before build. Keeping that split.
src/main/generated/assets/

# ...and the HashCache manifests are committed with it. The root .gitignore ignores every
# .cache/ directory, which silently defeated the split described above -- the manifests are
# what tells a build which generated files are supposed to exist, so they have to travel with
# the tree. They hold paths and hashes only, no asset bytes, and are byte-stable between runs
# (the date field in their header is a fixed sentinel, not a timestamp).
!src/main/generated/.cache/
